  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is negative or near-zero, especially after recent spikes.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following high historical prices (e.g., >75) by applying a 5-10% dampening factor.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is >10% above recent 7-day average, reduce by 1-2% per day.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to sentiment when sentiment >0.3, especially in early-week cycles.",
    "Correct for lagged underestimation: if true outcome > forecast by >5% for 3+ consecutive days, adjust next forecast upward by 1-2%.",
    "Avoid overreacting to single-day sentiment spikes — apply smoothing filter (e.g., 3-day moving average) before final adjustment."
  ]
}
